---
import '../styles/global.css';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const canonical = new URL('/privacy/', site.url).href;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-skin="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy | {site.nameWithTitle}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="What this site stores, what it loads from other services, and how to get in touch." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#1c1916" />
    <script is:inline>
      try {
        var s = localStorage.getItem('skin');
        if (s === 'light' || s === 'dark') document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-skin', s);
      } catch (e) {}
    </script>
  </head>
  <body data-track="both">
    <main class="sec privacy">
      <a class="back" href="/">Back to the portfolio</a>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 1 November 2026</p>

      <p>This is the personal website of {site.name}. It has no accounts, forms, comments or shop, and it does not collect personal information.</p>

      <h2>Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
      <p>The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics, advertising or tracking tools. Its fonts and images are served from this site, not from third parties.</p>

      <h2>What your browser stores</h2>
      <p>If you switch between the dark and light skin, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage under <code>skin</code> so the site remembers it. A session flag, <code>floorWave</code>, stops the opening animation replaying during the same visit. Neither leaves your device, and clearing this site's data in your browser removes both.</p>

      <h2>Videos</h2>
      <p>The project demos are hosted on YouTube. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you press play; the player then loads from youtube-nocookie.com, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> applies to it.</p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs each visitor's IP address for security purposes; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages#data-collection">GitHub Pages data collection</a> and the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.</p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>Links to LinkedIn, Google Scholar, GitHub and YouTube take you to those services, which have their own privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
